<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">raise-wraith</ansi> spell

The <ansi fg="command">Raise Wraith</ansi> spell tears the lingering spirit from a corpse and
binds it into an ethereal form — half ghost, half hunger. Wraiths are
difficult to strike and sap the will of those they wound. Only a creature of
considerable essence can sustain this transformation.

Wraiths are swift, ethereal spellcasters that manifest eldritch magics. They
evade physical attacks with unnatural grace and assault foes with magical
assaults from beyond the veil.

The undead servant's power scales with your willpower and spellcasting skill.
More skilled casters raise more formidable specimens.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast raise-wraith [corpse]</ansi>     Animate nearby remains.

<ansi fg="yellow">Base Folds:  </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">8</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Corpse:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Requires substantial remains</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Target:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Nearby corpse or ground loot</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Conv. Cost:  </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">45</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">School:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Manifestation</ansi>

<ansi fg="white-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - The wraith appears under your command and aids you in combat.
  - Once raised, the undead servant remains active as a companion.
  - Use the <ansi fg="command">assess</ansi> command to evaluate a corpse's quality.

